{"skill":{"slug":"facebook-pages","displayName":"Facebook"},"version":{"version":"1.0.7","createdAt":1791056443316,"changelog":"Security section now states that the public-data tools read other people's public content without a connected account (read-only, paid from credit).","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":14970,"sha256":"b760e7a2646617344d19feed37c4d3deaf77db25f9a9d7b4055e32b2c656ff75","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1948,"sha256":"1caa63aec20b9239f729cc49c5f9a6e6456d781468946eb6318f0fb121e9eec4","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1791060186099,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5b1382297a3b59efbec4a23d0b3bbce27dccb5c9f3e99f9f550ddd602f050c34","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5b1382297a3b59efbec4a23d0b3bbce27dccb5c9f3e99f9f550ddd602f050c34","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1791060109193},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":17,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1791060186099},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed Facebook Pages integration that uses ClawLink OAuth and requires confirmation before posting, messaging, updating, or deleting content.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill uses hosted ClawLink OAuth and paid public-data calls, which is proportionate for Facebook integration work but means users should understand ClawLink will broker requests and hold tokens.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation asks the user to install the ClawLink plugin, allow it in OpenClaw configuration, and restart the gateway; this is disclosed and purpose-aligned but grants the integration plugin runtime access.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions tell the agent to discover live tools, preview unfamiliar or write operations, and require explicit user confirmation before create, update, delete, publish, or messaging actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No bundled executable code, background worker, local credential-file access, or persistence hook is present in the artifact; the persistent element is the normal installed plugin/config and remote OAuth connection.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The capabilities match the stated purpose: reading Facebook Page data, public Facebook data, metrics, comments, messages, and performing Page write actions through Facebook/ClawLink tools.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want ClawLink to connect to Facebook on your behalf. Review OAuth permissions in the ClawLink/Facebook flow, watch for paid public-data calls, and confirm every public post, message, update, or delete before execution.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The scanner flagged the phrase 'access token' in a troubleshooting table, but the artifact does not instruct the agent to read credential files or extract tokens; it explains OAuth token expiry and reconnection through ClawLink.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1791060186099}}}}}